sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/maynardsmith-twofold-cost> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Twofold cost of sex (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "With equal fecundity, a 1:1 sex ratio and males contributing nothing, the odds of asexual to sexual females double every generation and are 2^n times the initial odds after n generations." ;
    dct:source "The Evolution of Sex (1978)" ;
    skos:notation "with equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio, the odds of asexual to sexual females double each generation: \\frac{q_{t+1}}{1-q_{t+1}} = 2\\frac{q_t}{1-q_t}" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Twofold cost of sex.** With equal fecundity and a `1 : 1` sex ratio, the odds of asexual to sexual females double every generation. Fecundity cancels. -/
theorem twofold_cost_of_sex {q f : ℝ} (hq0 : 0 < q) (hq1 : q < 1) (hf : 0 < f) :
    odds (asexualNext q f) = 2 * odds q"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.asexualNext" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.twofold_cost_of_sex", "Delphi.twofold_cost_of_sex_n" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Deterministic odds identity under equal fecundity, 1:1 sex ratio and males contributing nothing; iterated form gives odds x 2^n after n generations." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/Delphi/MaynardSmith.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-twofold-cost> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/maynardsmith-twofold-cost> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-maynardsmith-twofold-cost> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-maynardsmith-twofold-cost> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.twofold_cost_of_sex with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/MaynardSmith.lean (110 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.twofold_cost_of_sex, Delphi.twofold_cost_of_sex_n: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T16:36:18.727Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [maynardsmith-threefold] Statement changed to claim the odds triple each generation instead of doubling. Rejected with 2 error(s): maynardsmith-threefold.lean:59:43: error: unsolved goals Controls: 7 of 7 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/maynardsmith-twofold-cost> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/main/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

